# Build-context ignores for the frontend image (context = ./cv-analyzer-frontend).
#
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, Docker patterns are anchored at the context root.
# Use a `**/` prefix for anything that can appear at any depth.

# --- Dependencies: installed fresh by `npm ci` inside the image -----------
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build output & tool caches: regenerated by `npm run build` -----------
.next
out
dist
build
.eslintcache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Secrets & local config: never bake into an image ----------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values arrive via Docker build args (see docker-compose.*.yml)
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- VCS / editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Docs (not part of the app) -------------------------------------------
**/*.md
docs

# --- Build files -----------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded from COPY so that editing the Dockerfile doesn't bust the
# source-copy layer. Docker still reads both files itself to run the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
